    description: "Seen in the cron test-agent-infra log 2026-10-14: with pytest-cov missing, pytest rejected --cov (exit 4) and smart-test's summary still printed 'COVERAGE: (all files at 100%)'. The exit code stayed non-zero, so nothing passed falsely, but the summary claims coverage for a run that measured nothing. count_executed_tests returns 'unknown' when there is neither a junit file nor a result line, so zero_run stays false. Fix: no coverage section unless a coverage TOTAL line exists; say 'pytest did not run (exit 4: usage error)'."  # c205
